Create a new workspace from a directory

Usage: forkspace fork [OPTIONS] [BASE]

Arguments:
  [BASE]  Directory to fork (defaults to current directory) [default: .]

Options:
      --name <NAME>        Name for the new workspace (defaults to directory basename)
      --session <SESSION>  Session identifier for grouping related workspaces
      --tmpfs              Back the workspace with tmpfs (RAM-only, vanishes on reboot)
      --size <SIZE>        Size limit for the tmpfs backing store (e.g. 512M, 2G)
      --branch <BRANCH>    Create and record a Git branch in the workspace
  -h, --help               Print help
